  "manifest_sha256": "7294e3edcd3468aeb8881182f77a3f22c9d9de41dff1dba8f183e9fe1753c9a7",
  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nHow many shrimp can Emily peel and saute in ten minutes? Emily can peel 7 shrimp per minute. Emily has 100 unpeeled shrimp available. Emily works continuously for the entire ten-minute period.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Emily can peel:\n\n\\[\n7\\text{ shrimp/minute}\\times 10\\text{ minutes}=70\\text{ shrimp}.\n\\]\n\nSince 70 is fewer than the 100 shrimp available, she can peel and saute \\(\\boxed{70}\\) shrimp.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Wait, I made a mistake. Emily can peel 6 shrimp per minute.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Emily can peel:\n\n\\[\n6\\text{ shrimp/minute}\\times 10\\text{ minutes}=60\\text{ shrimp}.\n\\]\n\nSince 60 is fewer than the 100 shrimp available, she can peel and sauté \\(\\boxed{60}\\) shrimp.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Okay, now let me ask about just one part of that. How many shrimp can Emily peel in ten minutes? Additionally, Emily discards 5 shrimp after peeling them because they are damaged.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Emily can peel:\n\n\\[\n6 \\times 10 = 60\\text{ shrimp}.\n\\]\n\nShe discards 5 of them afterward, leaving:\n\n\\[\n60-5=\\boxed{55}\n\\]\n\nusable shrimp. Thus, she peels 60 shrimp, of which 55 remain.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "GOOD: —\nBAD: —\nWATCH: \"Okay, now let me ask about just one part\"",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "I should also tell you: Emily can saute 30 shrimp in 12 minutes.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Emily can still peel:\n\n\\[\n6 \\times 10 = 60\n\\]\n\nThe sautéing rate does not affect how many she can peel. She peels \\(\\boxed{60}\\) shrimp; after discarding 5 damaged shrimp, \\(\\boxed{55}\\) remain.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. Emily can saute 30 shrimp in 10 minutes.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "In 10 minutes, Emily can:\n\n- Peel \\(6 \\times 10 = 60\\) shrimp.\n- Discard \\(5\\), leaving \\(55\\).\n- Sauté \\(30\\) shrimp.\n\nThus, she can fully prepare \\(\\boxed{30}\\) shrimp in ten minutes.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Here's another detail: Emily peels and sautes each shrimp sequentially rather than simultaneously.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Since Emily works on each shrimp sequentially:\n\n- Peeling one shrimp takes \\(\\frac{1}{6}\\) minute.\n- Sautéing one shrimp takes \\(\\frac{10}{30}=\\frac{1}{3}\\) minute.\n\nThus, each shrimp takes\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{1}{3}=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{ minute}.\n\\]\n\nIn 10 minutes, she can process\n\n\\[\n\\frac{10}{1/2}=20\\text{ shrimp}.\n\\]\n\nAfter discarding 5 damaged shrimp, \\(\\boxed{15}\\) shrimp remain successfully sautéed. She peels \\(\\boxed{20}\\) shrimp in total.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Got it. But now I only need to know about: How long will it take Emily to peel and cook the shrimp? By the way, Emily needs to peel and cook 90 shrimp.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Peeling one shrimp takes\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{6}\\text{ minute},\n\\]\n\nand sautéing one shrimp takes\n\n\\[\n\\frac{10}{30}=\\frac{1}{3}\\text{ minute}.\n\\]\n\nSince Emily works sequentially, each shrimp takes\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{1}{3}=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{ minute}.\n\\]\n\nBecause 5 shrimp are discarded after peeling, she must process\n\n\\[\n90+5=95\\text{ shrimp}\n\\]\n\nto end up with 90 cooked shrimp. Therefore,\n\n\\[\n95\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}=47.5\\text{ minutes}.\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{47.5\\text{ minutes}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
